<title>UK: Sutton Harbour shares make AIM debut.</title>
<headline>Sutton Harbour shares make AIM debut.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Devon-based property developer Sutton Harbour Holdings Plc made their debut on the Alternative Investment Market (AIM) on Monday.</p>
<p>By 1000 GMT the shares were quoted at 125p, although no trade was registered in the stock.</p>
<p>The shares were previously traded on Ofex, the public trading facility managed by brokerage JP Jenkins which allows dealings in unquoted companies.</p>
<p>Bristol-based brokerage Rowan Dartington, which introduced the company to AIM, said the shares were last traded on Ofex at about 120p, valuing the company at 12.0 million stg.</p>
<p>The company raised no new money with the listing.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7945</p>
</text>
